"""
Short values sealed in the token form of version 0xCC that Go
implementations of Fernet write, so that Wolly reads and writes what they keep: a key of
48 bytes, written as URL Base64 with padding, is a signing key of 16 bytes
and an encryption key of 32.

A token is 0xCC, the time in seconds as 8 bytes big endian, a nonce of 24
random bytes, the XChaCha20-Poly1305 ciphertext of the value with the
first 9 bytes as associated data, and the HMAC-SHA3-512 of all that under
the signing key.  open checks the HMAC first, in constant time, then the
ciphertext; a token of another version is refused.  The time is written
but never checked: a sealed value has no age limit.
"""
import Standard.String (
    String,
    length
);

module Wolly.Fernet is
    """
    The bytes a token adds to its value: 1 + 8 + 24 + 16 + 64.
    """
    function overheadBytes(): Index
        ensures result = 113;

    """
    The two keys of keyText, the URL Base64 of 48 bytes.  None for text of
    another form.
    No contract: an Option read from text.
    """
    generic [K: Region]
    function readFernetKey(keyText: Span[Nat8, K]): Option[String];

    """
    A new key: 48 random bytes in URL Base64 with padding.  None when the
    random source fails.
    No contract: an Option over the random source.
    """
    function newFernetKey(): Option[String];

    """
    The token of value under the key keyText at the time now.  None when
    keyText is no key, the random source or libcrypto fails.  No ensures:
    an Option over the random source.
    """
    generic [K: Region, V: Region]
    function sealFernet(keyText: Span[Nat8, K], value: Span[Nat8, V], now: Int64): Option[String]
        requires now >= 0;

    """
    The value of token under the key keyText.  None when keyText is no key,
    token is not of version 0xCC or too short, its HMAC or its ciphertext
    does not hold.
    No contract: an Option read from a token.
    """
    generic [K: Region, T: Region]
    function openFernet(keyText: Span[Nat8, K], token: Span[Nat8, T]): Option[String];
end module.
